# 7. Preventing duplicate payments

## Problem

The user clicks the Pay button twice, or the mobile app retries the same request because of poor network connectivity.

Without protection:

```text
Request 1 → Debit ₹500
Request 2 → Debit ₹500
```

The user could lose ₹1,000 instead of ₹500.

## Solution: Idempotency key

The client sends a unique key with every payment request.

```http
POST /api/payments
Idempotency-Key: REQ-12345
```

The backend checks whether the key already exists.

```text
If key does not exist:
    Create payment and process it

If key already exists:
    Return the previous payment result
```

Database constraint:

```text
UNIQUE(idempotency_key)
```

Interview answer:

> Idempotency ensures that retrying the same payment request does not create multiple financial transactions.

