# 9. Scaling the system

PhonePe must support large numbers of concurrent users and transactions. PhonePe has publicly described using database sharding and a shared-nothing approach to avoid a single database becoming a bottleneck. ([PhonePe][2])

## Scaling architecture

```text
                 ┌──────────────┐
                 │ Load Balancer│
                 └──────┬───────┘
                        │
          ┌─────────────┼─────────────┐
          ▼             ▼             ▼
     Backend 1     Backend 2     Backend 3
          │             │             │
          └─────────────┼─────────────┘
                        │
                ┌───────┴────────┐
                ▼                ▼
          Payment DB        Redis Cache
                │
                ▼
          Message Queue
                │
                ▼
          Worker Services
```

### Important scaling techniques

| Technique          | Purpose                                     |
| ------------------ | ------------------------------------------- |
| Load Balancer      | Distributes traffic                         |
| Horizontal Scaling | Adds more backend servers                   |
| Database Sharding  | Splits data across databases                |
| Read Replicas      | Handles read-heavy queries                  |
| Redis              | Reduces database reads                      |
| Message Queue      | Processes background tasks                  |
| Auto Scaling       | Adds/removes servers based on load          |
| Rate Limiting      | Prevents abuse and overload                 |
| Circuit Breaker    | Prevents repeated calls to failing services |

