# 10. Database sharding

Suppose we have 500 million users.

Using one database may create a bottleneck. We can distribute users across shards.

```text
User ID Hash
     │
     ▼
Hash Function
     │
 ┌───┼────┬────┐
 ▼   ▼    ▼    ▼
DB-1 DB-2 DB-3 DB-4
```

Example:

```javascript
shardNumber = hash(userId) % 4;
```

Possible distribution:

```text
Hash(USER101) % 4 = 0 → DB-1
Hash(USER102) % 4 = 2 → DB-3
Hash(USER103) % 4 = 1 → DB-2
```

For production systems, consistent hashing or a carefully managed shard-mapping strategy may be used to reduce data movement during resharding.

